body: |-
  BUILD METHOD: design panel (Arky/Loid/Jinx/Aegis, TD-071) → foundation build + verify → live-half build + verify → Aegis security review (found 1 blocking injection gap + 2 unwired-gate gaps) → gap fixes + verify → Aegis re-review CLEARED. Every increment independently verified (tsc + tests) before commit; the security review caught a real filePath/failingCheck injection channel the twin was blind to.

  CLEARED with two conditions/notes:
  - OPERATIONAL (not a code gap): the run procedure MUST `git commit` the witness head (ledger.head() → the git-tracked witness file) BEFORE any Warpline verdict is joined — the external-witness tamper-evidence binds against the incentivized owner only once committed. The runner writes+reminds; the operator commits.
  - BACKLOG (minor, non-blocking): (a) neutralizeField truncates the twin path at the first control byte while sanitizeField escapes-in-place at render → hostile card and twin carry slightly different BENIGN residual path text (harmless; escape-vs-truncate if byte-parity ever wanted); (b) parseLabel substring fallback on the model's own output (mitigated by temp 0 / N=3 / 'nothing else').

  REMAINING before the judge runs live: a runner that walks the Expo audit rows/KNOTs → cards → runJudgeEnforced → scoring (Arky file-plan step 7, the field-test wiring), and the real-API regression over case-13/case-20 (behind WARPLINE_JUDGE_LIVE). These are run-wiring, not instrument-build.

  NEXT PATH ITEM: the two engine pre-fixes the judge measures — Tier-0 invariant false-CLEAN (T-2026-06-24-015) and essence-hash over-block false-KNOT (T-2026-07-15-008). Design pass underway.
